# Architecture

Follow [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md). Layer rules: [backend/CONVENTIONS.md](backend/CONVENTIONS.md), [frontend/CONVENTIONS.md](frontend/CONVENTIONS.md).

- Three processes: api (HTTP + SSE + Queue.add), worker (BullMQ + media), web (SPA). Never run ffmpeg in api. Never `new Worker` in api.
- MySQL = durable state. Redis = queues, cancel flags, progress. Do not write per-percent progress to MySQL.
- One SSE connection per browser tab (`GET /api/events`). No client `setInterval` polling. No WebSocket for progress. No EventSource per card (HTTP/1.1 ~6 connections/origin).
- New backend code goes in `backend/src/modules/*` as feature folders. New frontend code goes in `frontend/src/features/*`. Do not grow `App.tsx` or `routes/users.ts` as the pattern.
- Shared queue names and job DTOs live in one module (`backend/src/shared`, `queue-names.ts`). Do not duplicate queue name strings.
- Learning code (`bullMQjobs`, queue `buttonClick`, QueueCard in App) is sandbox. Product modules must not import it.
